{"type":"text","timestamp":1794546734187,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb172abffelzYZkz2FqDnqf9","part":{"id":"prt_1d3520aac0016iyhqyoUUoioLE","sessionID":"ses_e2cb172abffelzYZkz2FqDnqf9","messageID":"msg_1d351fe3e001UCr60AwQLLxOrH","type":"text","text":"T039 is complete and the checkbox is left unticked. The build ran first and all verify commands pass.\n\n**Files written**\n\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`: `cliRecommendations` now spreads `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` and `needsMode` onto each mapped recommendation, with the rationale comment.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts`: added the `it.each` case with the skill row and the hub row.\n- No other files changed. `git status --short` lists only those two files, and the dist tree reports no tracked changes.\n\n**Build and verify output**\n\n```\nnpm run build  (in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime)\nexit=0\n\nrg -c \"needsMode\" $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/render.js\n1\n\nVPL\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  97 passed (97)\n\nNPL\nℹ tests 42\nℹ pass 42\nℹ fail 0\n\nnode --check $PLG\nexit=0\n\nrg -c \"recommendation\\.(command|policy|ownerSkillId|needsMode)\" $PLG\n4\n\nnode $SP/planning/probe-opencode-brief.mjs --fixture | rg -c \"opencode plugin names command=true names policy=true\"\n1\n\nSRM\nexit=0\n[runtime-mirror-sync] PASS: 256 mirrors across 10 trees are in sync.\n\nreadlink .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js\n../../../../.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js\n```\n\nBefore the mapper edit, VPL reported exactly 2 failed, matching the task. After the edit it reports 97 passed and 0 failed.\n\n**One deviation to record**\n\nThe probe inherits this worker's `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, and the renderer deliberately renders a child session's command as `(parent-named only)`, so the raw probe prints `names policy=false` and the count is 0. Ran with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD`, the fixture head is `Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.` and the count is 1. This is the same cause the brief warned about for vitest.\n\nNothing is blocked on the operator.","time":{"start":1794546731692,"end":1794546734187}}}
